{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/113176-could-a-changeling-detect-a-demon-s-lies","id":113176,"title":"Could a Changeling detect a Demon's lies?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-15T00:40:13-07:00","id":113176,"title":"Could a Changeling detect a Demon's lies?","content":"I know that might be a weird question, but let's say a Changeling is somewhat aware of a Demon's nature (emphasis on somewhat) and tricks the Demon into a pledge where the Demon must convey everything it knows truthfully or face the sanction of the pledge. <br /> <br /> Since pledges are woven into the tapestry of Fate itself, would it be able to detect the Demon's lies despite the Demon's mind being disconnected to its body? Would the Changeling in question, despite not knowing the specifics, be able to gauge the lies of a Demon by the activation of the Sanction?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T00:52:30-07:00","id":113183,"title":"","content":"Purely IMO:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hellovg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/113176-could-a-changeling-detect-a-demon-s-lies#post113176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since pledges are woven into the tapestry of Fate itself, would it be able to detect the Demon's lies despite the Demon's mind being disconnected to its body?</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hellovg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/113176-could-a-changeling-detect-a-demon-s-lies#post113176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would the Changeling in question, despite not knowing the specifics, be able to gauge the lies of a Demon by the activation of the Sanction?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, if the sanction had some component the Changeling could sense.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T03:43:05-07:00","id":113227,"title":"","content":"I think Pledges might be somewhat complicated by the factors of demonic Pacts. I think there should be some unusual interaction--for example, a demon should recognize when it is being offered an oath, and vice versa for the changeling and pacts. Demons would be savvy at negociations once they are aware of what is going on. Either way, I'd say that, no, the changeling cannot detect it via the Pledge due to that disconnect--the pledge was made with the demon, while the lie is spoken by the Cover. If the sanction triggers, I'd say it'd a) not be noticed by the changeling if it occurs immediately, or b) &quot;hang&quot; until the demon enters demonic form (as it was the demon that broke the pledge), thus rendering it unable to tell exactly what statement was the lie that triggered it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T06:15:50-07:00","id":113286,"title":"","content":"The answer: No, they cannot (pg. 183)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Assistant Organizer for:</b><br /> <a href=\"http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i162.photobucket.com/albums/t261/jlburgos_bucket/a41e98d1-1eed-4506-a8d2-2b3bea4a43da_zps469395ad.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":311,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/311-joeb","user":"JoeB","date":". 04-15-2014, 09:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/311-joeb","name":"JoeB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar311_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T09:30:57-07:00","id":113377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JoeB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/113176-could-a-changeling-detect-a-demon-s-lies?p=113286#post113286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The answer: No, they cannot (pg. 183)</div> </div> </div> </div>What is the point of the Subterfuge skill if the demon can do that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2448-dante","name":"Dante","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T11:06:34-07:00","id":113429,"title":"","content":"I would call for a clash of wills. If the demon won, he could lie his face off and the pledge would do nothing. Otherwise, the pledge breaks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T11:12:56-07:00","id":113432,"title":"","content":"Just because you can say &quot;The Sky is Orange&quot; with a straight face and a quantum truth qualifier doesn't mean people will believe you when you say it.<br /> <br /> Subterfuge is for telling a convincing lie, something that body language and quantum truth status can help with but can't wholly do the job there of.<br /> <br /> As for the main question, it depends. If you trap a demon in a pledge to tell the truth, it kind of depends on if the Wyrd can read their intent or not. Given that it's the Wyrd, it's flexible enough to warrant a &quot;at the storyteller's discretion&quot;. On the one hand, the demon promised ot tell the truth, and even though what it says comes across as true, the demon is learly lying to the Eye or the Wyrd....on the other hand, the Wyrd connects the statements to whatever and finds them true, so it's all good.<br /> <br /> If I had to pick one, it's probably the former actually, since the wording of a contract is in effect changing how reality interacts with you and others for the duration-it's temporarily suspending the effects of the demon's quantum engines through loopholes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T11:58:38-07:00","id":113462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/113176-could-a-changeling-detect-a-demon-s-lies?p=113432#post113432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Subterfuge is for telling a convincing lie, something that body language and quantum truth status can help with but can't wholly do the job there of.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, the Skill serves more purposes than just &quot;tell lies&quot; - it's the disguise Skill, which is kind of hella important when Alternate Identity is such a valuable Merit for the Unchained.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T11:59:26-07:00","id":113463,"title":"","content":"I would think that's in the &quot;messes with template, can't be done till tier 4&quot; ruling. Changelings cant give or take a vampire's sunlight weaknesses, or modifying a mage's paradox. while i wouldnt allow a pledge to easily let a changeling sense if a demon is lying, I'd allow a clever changeling to use the Pledge as the center of a Voitkampf like Mages do to tell if the creature is a demon. I'd say when a central template trait and a non tier 4 side power go head to head, I favor the central template trait. It can be justified in various ways IC, but I'd still hold true to the established precedents. whether its because the wyrd is the GM, demonic soul/mind duality, because of technicalities and loopholes involved in pledging a demon, etc. To figure out a demon or angel's lies, you've gotta do your research and outsmart them. No power should unlock it, when the core specifically states that even supernatural attempts fail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T12:12:20-07:00","id":113472,"title":"","content":"Again, it depends on what you see the Wyrd hooking onto-the intent of the lie or the lie itself. Primum only affects consciously decided self-manifestations(ie, what a demon communicates directly) and doesn't touch something hitting their intent unless they say something about it. I think that's enough of a loophole for the Wyrd to exploit, but others might not think so.<br /> <br /> We could sit here and talk metaphysics of demon's advanced laws and the effect of their quantum engine/brain versus the meta-connectivity of the Wyrd and how changelings use it, but That can get boring real quick. I don't think it's strictly a Tier 4 thing if it makes sense to the storyteller otherwise, but it comes down to the storyteller.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T13:20:00-07:00","id":113509,"title":"","content":"Whatever the storyteller chooses, they should be consistent. So the question is: is the oath broken when the oath-breaker /thinks/ its broken, or when reality thinks its broken.<br /> <br /> I think of it like this: Demon's are good at lying because they can convince themselves on a basic level that a lie is the truth, not because they can change reality to make a lie the truth. <br /> <br /> I haven't read through all of changelings rules. Can you accidentally break an oath? If you can, then no amount of changing your bodies personal belief can change the fact that you broke an oath.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T13:27:38-07:00","id":113512,"title":"","content":"Fair enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-15T13:32:54-07:00","id":113516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oddness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/113176-could-a-changeling-detect-a-demon-s-lies?p=113509#post113509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think of it like this: Demon's are good at lying because they can convince themselves on a basic level that a lie is the truth, not because they can change reality to make a lie the truth.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's linguistic/semantic jiggery-pokery, not self-deception or reality-warping. The fact that there are at least <i>three</i> Embeds whose effect can be described as &quot;make words not mean things&quot; in the corebook alone, along with the fact that the one exception to the ability is that demons can't lie in writing in the composition of a pact, would kind of indicate that messing with meaning is a thing the Unchained do.<br /> <br /> &quot;Even a power that detects <i>whether a statement is true</i> rather than <i>whether the speaking is deliberately lying</i> still fails to work reliably against one of the Unchained. A statement will read as true if the demon says it is.&quot;<br /> <br /> To the best of my knowledge, the former type of power only exists in Changeling, where it's a one-dot Goblin Contract.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I haven't read through all of changelings rules. Can you accidentally break an oath? </div> </div> </div>Considering that one of the few speculated ways to kill the Fae is to make it break a Namebound oath - which they are <i>constitutionally incapable of deliberately breaking</i> - it would be rather bizarre if you couldn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T06:28:21-07:00","id":114006,"title":"","content":"Interesting.<br /> <br /> My understanding (getting into the metaphysics of demons, doh) is that the reason that demons are so good at lying is because they have such perfect control of their covers. They can literally control the perceived reality of their cover. So if a demon tells his cover that up is down, the cover starts flying into the sky (theoretically, in reality the cover would glitch out and be blown pretty much immediately since the idea clashes with the framework of reality and there's no embedded loophole in reality to let this happen)<br /> <br /> I think I'd run it like this: when making a pact, the demon has a choice. Is he personally making the pact, or is his cover making the pact? If he makes it, there's no problems and everything proceeds as if a regular human made the pact. If his cover makes it? Then the demon must begin spoofing the changeling the same way an angel might, or the changeling might detect that the pact doesn't hold any water and nullify it without consequence. If the cover breaks the pact, the demon can dictate that as far as the cover is concerned the pact isn't broken, but now he must spoof the changeling every hour or so, probably at a major disadvantage. As far as the changeling is concerned, the pact is broken when the cover is destroyed or when the demon decides to stop denying that the pact is broken for that cover - in which case the cover would take on the repercussions of breaking the pact. Even if the changeling were to get physical evidence that the pact had been broken, as long as the cover holds up the pact still holds. I think this holds to the spirit of Demon, although I'm not sure how true to the idea of changeling this holds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T06:29:07-07:00","id":114009,"title":"","content":"Actually, the more I think on it, I'm going to change my answer to &quot;the demon wins.&quot; The pledge is no different than any other power in the world that can pull this off, and being a perfect liar is as much part of being a demon as using dreams are to a changeling.<br /> <br /> <br /> I don't like the idea that there's any power out there than can completely get past such an inextricable part of a supernatural's nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 04-16-2014, 09:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T08:54:45-07:00","id":114106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/113176-could-a-changeling-detect-a-demon-s-lies?p=114009#post114009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, the more I think on it, I'm going to change my answer to &quot;the demon wins.&quot; The pledge is no different than any other power in the world that can pull this off, and being a perfect liar is as much part of being a demon as using dreams are to a changeling.<br /> <br /> <br /> I don't like the idea that there's any power out there than can completely get past such an inextricable part of a supernatural's nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I think if you make the demon immune to all forms of discovery, you destroy the central themes of demon. Angels have innate ways to find demons - why can't changelings have sly ways of finding them? I think it fits into both themes of the games.<br /> <br /> Besides, by saying that the demon just simply wins, sure you preserve a core characteristic of demon, but you destroy a core characteristic of changelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T12:44:18-07:00","id":114261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oddness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/113176-could-a-changeling-detect-a-demon-s-lies?p=114106#post114106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, I think if you make the demon immune to all forms of discovery, you destroy the central themes of demon. Angels have innate ways to find demons - why can't changelings have sly ways of finding them? I think it fits into both themes of the games.<br /> <br /> Besides, by saying that the demon just simply wins, sure you preserve a core characteristic of demon, but you destroy a core characteristic of changelings.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a conundrum isn't it? I wonder what the white wolf authors would say...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T12:51:40-07:00","id":114268,"title":"","content":"Personally I would rule that if the pledge was sworn while in cover it's perfectly fine, the demon gets away with it, the COVER swore and the demon decides what they believe, if the demon swore in it's natural form, or as itself, then all bets are off, any attempt at telling a lie would break the pledge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T14:19:14-07:00","id":114326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oddness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/113176-could-a-changeling-detect-a-demon-s-lies?p=114106#post114106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Eh, I think if you make by demon immune to all forms of discovery, you destroy the central themes of demon. Angels have innate ways to find demons - why can't changelings have sly ways of finding them? I think it fits into both themes of the games. Besides, by saying that the demon just simply wins, sure you preserve a core characteristic of demon, but you destroy a core characteristic of changelings.</div> </div> </div> </div> Angels don't hunt demons by hunting down liars, they usually have to wait for the demon to mess up IE tell a lie that the angel knows is factually untrue, or to burn aether around the right cryptid bloodhounds. And I ddon't think this destroys a core characteristic of changelings. Being a perfect liar is literally part of the demonic template. being able to see through lies perfectly is NOT part of the changeling template. Imagine if a Demonic exploit removed all of a changeling's pledge crafting or one I romantic powers. Kinda the same thing. A changeling can make pledges with a demon and have them work, but core Template abilities require tier 4 to alter. If you want a perfect pact that keeps a demon Honest, better find a true fae to make that bargain with the demon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T20:53:38-07:00","id":114518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asaram</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/113176-could-a-changeling-detect-a-demon-s-lies?p=114268#post114268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I would rule that if the pledge was sworn while in cover it's perfectly fine, the demon gets away with it, the COVER swore and the demon decides what they believe, if the demon swore in it's natural form, or as itself, then all bets are off, any attempt at telling a lie would break the pledge.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This answer is what makes the most sense in terms of gameplay\u2026at least to me!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-16T21:49:49-07:00","id":114541,"title":"","content":"When dealing with non-Changelings, the changeling doesn't have to make the sanction known when the pledge is made. The changeling can name it when the pledge is broken.<br /> So if the demon lies, and the changeling knows it (the sun is purple), the changeling can call upon a sanction at the time, for example, when they know the Demon has said a lie, even if they didn't use their skills to do so (he's a good liar, but he's definitely lying). Other supernaturals are considered human, in regards to pledges. Making a pledge with a demon to tell the truth to the changeling (or even everyone they come across) isn't really taking away their innate power, pledges don't work in regards to unfair stuff (hold your breath for a billion years, mortal). In this case, as Cleverest of Things pointed out, Angels don't hunt demons by hunting down liars, the Demon has a choice, whether to lie or not, his ability to do so is never taken away.<br /> <br /> That said, if you've been around the forums a bit you've probably noticed the ruling, something to the extent of, &quot;Your favorite splat gets the benefit of the doubt,&quot; which often plays second fiddle to, &quot;Do whatever's best for the game.&quot; Depending upon your game, who's doing the pledges, you might have the Wyrd (which is not a thing, mind, but the relationship between all things) patter uselessly off of them like water off a duck's back, or give the Demon a sense of repercussions of a less God Machine bent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-17-2014, 12:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-17T05:55:42-07:00","id":114671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dante</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/113176-could-a-changeling-detect-a-demon-s-lies?p=113377#post113377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the point of the Subterfuge skill if the demon can do that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Its explained in the rules, again, see pg. 183. If you are asking here then that is the answer. Of course, you can so as you please in your games (and if you want to crossover with Changeling).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Assistant Organizer for:</b><br /> <a href=\"http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i162.photobucket.com/albums/t261/jlburgos_bucket/a41e98d1-1eed-4506-a8d2-2b3bea4a43da_zps469395ad.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/311-joeb","name":"JoeB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar311_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-17T07:56:32-07:00","id":114709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oddness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/113176-could-a-changeling-detect-a-demon-s-lies?p=114106#post114106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, I think if you make the demon immune to all forms of discovery, you destroy the central themes of demon. Angels have innate ways to find demons - why can't changelings have sly ways of finding them? I think it fits into both themes of the games.</div> </div> </div> </div> Which involves forcing them to reveal their nature after they do something suspicious to draw attention to yourself. Its degrading their Cover until they can no longer do it.<br /> <br /> In either case detecting a demon or his lies are two different things. The first case has very specific rules, and requires a successful Cover roll - which is why angels do their best to force Compromise checks, and degrade cover until that Cover is either not functional, or has enough Conditions that Cover no longer works.<br /> <br /> The no-lying/mind reading thing just flat out negates any attempt to magically force someone to reveal the truth. And such a changeling pledge is just another magical truth power. If a changeling wanted to discover a demons true nature, they could investigate and track down information about it, just like mortals, angels, and every other supernatural on the planet. The changeling also has the advantage of dream invasions, tricky pledges, and their own Masks.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Besides, by saying that the demon just simply wins, sure you preserve a core characteristic of demon, but you destroy a core characteristic of changelings. </div> </div> </div> This doesn't negate a changeling's innate ability to manipulate the Mask, play with dreams, or to use their pledge magic. It negates a single, non-standard application of changeling pledge magic. The changeling could force a demon into an alliance (which IS a standard pledge to make) through pledges, and his lies won't protect him from breaking that. The changeling can make any other number of casual deals. It doesn't negate anything about changeling's themes, just one minor application that's being trying to be used to negate someone else's major aspects.<br /> <br /> I mean, by this rationale, a mage should be able to detect a demon's lies, because casting magic and gathering information is what they do. And yet, the book notes it won't work on demons. So, no. I don't think that pledges are any better than a mage spell, which cannot detect truth or lies.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT - the main Tasks that one can assign with a changeling pledge are : Alliance, Dreaming, Endeavor, Ensourcellment, and Forbiddance. Under suggested forbiddances, no where does it list &quot;lying&quot; or &quot;telling the truth&quot; as a suggestion. Using pledges to enforce truth is such a minor thing that allowing Unchained to avoid it has no impact on how changeling themes work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 04-17-2014, 12:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T11:02:56-07:00","id":116584,"title":"","content":"My opinion, contest Wyrd vs Cover. Since, they're both Supernaturals, the Unchained has a chance to deflect the attempt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T14:02:01-07:00","id":116677,"title":"","content":"My opinion, so long as the Demon decides that all of her statements are true, the pact would hold. If she makes a statement read as a lie, then the penalty clause lands.<br /> <br /> I'm more than a little uncomfortable with the idea that a <i>major</i> aspect of a template could be so easily subverted. Additionally, the book says that the Unchained actively decide the whether their words are true or not on the supernatural level. Plain and simple. Demon decides that her next statement will be the truth, it reads as true to any method of detection, natural or supernatural. The Wyrd doesn't get a fact-check, any more than a Mind or Dominate effect.<br /> Whether or not it's convincing is a whole different matter, one heavily dependent on context and ST input, thus outside of a mechanics debate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1424-ghanjrho","name":"GhanjRho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1424_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T19:48:21-07:00","id":116806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/113176-could-a-changeling-detect-a-demon-s-lies?p=113429#post113429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would call for a clash of wills. If the demon won, he could lie his face off and the pledge would do nothing. Otherwise, the pledge breaks.</div> </div> </div> </div>The deceptive power of demons is written as if it wouldn't actually trigger a Clash of Wills. So no, it doesn't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Besides, by saying that the demon just simply wins, sure you preserve a core characteristic of demon, but you destroy a core characteristic of changelings. </div> </div> </div>It tends to happen with crossover games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 04-20-2014, 10:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T22:19:31-07:00","id":116830,"title":"","content":"Personally, the fact that it ignores effects that tell whether something is true or not has still yet to make sense to me. You can perfectly mask all physical trances of lying. Fine. You can partition your mind in a way that even someone reading your mind is only shown what you want them to. Fine. Supernatural effects that ask magic/Wyrd/etc. that demons have no influence in whatsoever whether or not something is true are fooled. U wot m8?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T23:14:06-07:00","id":116837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/113176-could-a-changeling-detect-a-demon-s-lies?p=116830#post116830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, the fact that it ignores effects that tell whether something is true or not has still yet to make sense to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ignoring, for a moment, the lack of more than a single published power on the books that has that effect, those kinds of effects are already troublesome because a) [please do not make me go into brain-stabbing detail about how much knowledge of the supernatural is wrapped up in mythology and misdirection and broken-telephone/whisper-down-the-lane] and b) setting aside the preceding, such effects are themselves problematic from a &quot;fish for Real True Knowledge by asking random people about The World&quot; perspective to begin with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Supernatural effects that ask magic/Wyrd/etc. that demons have no influence in whatsoever whether or not something is true are fooled. U wot m8? </div> </div> </div>The power in question is literally the least expensive type of power for a changeling to gain access to that has a cost in experience and it's a power that, as with every other Contract, is a facet of the power behind a place where reality and the nature of truth is redefined on a moment-to-moment basis, and the Wyrd itself deals with forces associated with that big ball of from-a-certain-point-of-view narratively referred to as Prophecy Is A Lying Inconstant Sack Of Shit.<br /> <br /> The shortcuts the God-Machine has written into reality that the Unchained can still make use of include, among other things, the ability to sabotage Skill rolls by the broadcasting of misinformation that in common parlance is called <i>absolute horseshit</i>, along with the ability to produce generic instances of objects from empty space based purely on the notion that <i>nobody knew they weren't there before</i>.<br /> <br /> Inferno's been out for four years now, and Lord of Lies does much the same thing as Liar's Tongue, with an added sting: &quot;No supernatural power can detect a demon\u2019s lies, half-truths or other deceptions, even when the power does not depend upon reading the demon\u2019s \u201cmind.\u201d For example, powers that search for falsehood according to the threads of destiny (such as Awakened Fate spells) are useless. Anyone using such a power sees whatever the demon wants him to see.&quot;<br /> <br /> Did you wot all that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 04-21-2014, 02:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T23:25:50-07:00","id":116838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/113176-could-a-changeling-detect-a-demon-s-lies?p=116830#post116830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, the fact that it ignores effects that tell whether something is true or not has still yet to make sense to me. You can perfectly mask all physical trances of lying. Fine. You can partition your mind in a way that even someone reading your mind is only shown what you want them to. Fine. Supernatural effects that ask magic/Wyrd/etc. that demons have no influence in whatsoever whether or not something is true are fooled. U wot m8?</div> </div> </div> </div>The way I explain the last one is this: Demon's are bizarre quantum beings, made by a 4th or 5th dimensional entity and cobbled together from bits of that stolen multiverse. So when magic goes to check if something is &quot;true&quot; in regards to a demon, it's asking if it's true in a vaster sense that the user ever intended.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T23:39:14-07:00","id":116844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/113176-could-a-changeling-detect-a-demon-s-lies?p=116838#post116838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I explain the last one is this: Demon's are bizarre quantum beings, made by a 4th or 5th dimensional entity and cobbled together from bits of that stolen multiverse. So when magic goes to check if something is &quot;true&quot; in regards to a demon, it's asking if it's true in a vaster sense that the user ever intended.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea...still not really buying it. I'll accept that that's just how it works because the developers say so but it really reeks of...something, I can't quite think of a proper term to describe why it seems so off/forced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T04:31:53-07:00","id":116879,"title":"","content":"There's also a reverse problem. Their ability to lie isn't just a benefit, it's a problem for them socially, not to mention psychologically. Having a way round that would remove a lot of tension there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T04:42:37-07:00","id":116883,"title":"","content":"Short answer to the general question (provided on the 4th post in this thread) - <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JoeB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/113176-could-a-changeling-detect-a-demon-s-lies?p=113286#post113286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The answer: No, they cannot (pg. 183)</div> </div> </div> </div>Longer answer provided by general mechanics of the NWoD -<br /> <br /> No. Perfect lying is part of the Demon base template and those abilities cannot be negated until a game line reaches tier 4 (cosmic) level powers e.g. Archmages, Ascended True Fae, Rank 6+ Angels, Spirits etc. <br /> <br /> Even longer answer provided by in-game metaphysics -<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/113176-could-a-changeling-detect-a-demon-s-lies?p=113286#post113286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I explain the last one is this: Demon's are bizarre quantum beings, made by a 4th or 5th dimensional entity and cobbled together from bits of that stolen multiverse. So when magic goes to check if something is &quot;true&quot; in regards to a demon, it's asking if it's true in a vaster sense that the user ever intended.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically a Demon decides in the moment that they make a statement if it is actually &quot;true&quot; or &quot;false&quot; as far as the rest of reality is concerned. To use the example in the book, one of the Unchained decides that the statement<i> &quot;The sky is orange.&quot;</i> is &quot;true&quot; when they utter it. Anyone using any sort of truth detecting power has that statement ring as true. Anyone with any common sense will realize that the sky is not in fact orange, but may for example think that the Unchained really genuinely believes that to be the case. <br /> <br /> As several other posters have pointed out - Vampiric disciplines like Dominate and Auspex don't get a break in regards to this ability.<br /> <br /> Some of the contention on this point comes down to the wonderfully vague, narrative and ass-pully nature of the Wyrd. With the idea that Changelings are tapping into something beyond themselves that might be on a tier 4 level and therefore see through an Unchained's lie ability. Personally I'd ague a Changelings ability to interact with the Wyrd is not intricate or strong enough to do this.<br /> <br /> A comparison then might be with the Mind and Fate Arcana from Mage don't get a break in regard to the Unchained's lie ability. Considering the Arcana and the underlying principles of reality that Mages learn and they can't if a Demon is lying or not, I'm inclined to argue that the Wyrd is non the wiser either. <br /> <br /> The Shorter answer - <br /> <br /> If the ST wants Pledges to negate the Unchained's lying ability then it can. Because that's the general rule with all WoD rules calls cross-over or otherwise, the ST is the final arbiter. <br /> <br /> In such a case then its a matter of the themes of the game and the general taste one is going for in ones game. Want to play up the &quot;awesome cosmic power&quot; of the Wyrd, make it possible. Want to stress the &quot;never know who to trust&quot; theme of Demon, don't make it possible. <br /> <br /> Ultimately 9 times out of 10 it will come down to which game the ST likes more. My local Changeling ST would rule Pledges do curtail the lying ability. I'd rule that pledges don't negate the lying ability because I much prefer Demon as a game. <br /> <br /> The other 1 out of 10 times is the rule call purely for tone/game reasons. Which generally will go along with the &quot;no altering base template features before tier 4 powers&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T04:57:42-07:00","id":116891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/113176-could-a-changeling-detect-a-demon-s-lies?p=116806#post116806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The deceptive power of demons is written as if it wouldn't actually trigger a Clash of Wills. So no, it doesn't.</div> </div> </div> </div> Which is why I changed my mind in a later, more descriptive post. Just two up from yours, in fact.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/113176-could-a-changeling-detect-a-demon-s-lies?p=116844#post116844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yea...still not really buying it. I'll accept that that's just how it works because the developers say so but it really reeks of...something, I can't quite think of a proper term to describe why it seems so off/forced.</div> </div> </div> </div> Its not just the developers randomly saying things. Demons are liars by nature. Its a large part of what makes any demon a demon. That's just an in-game rationale for letting demons have demonic traits. Like Satchel said, Inferno has the same exact thing, with no more justification than &quot;These are demons.&quot;<br /> <br /> It may seem off to you because you just want there to be some way to break the whole perfect liar thing. Food for thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T07:12:52-07:00","id":116927,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm kinda convinced that you're right. I think the easiest explanation is the whole 'alternate dimensions' thing - The demon can say it's true for that cover because, in one of the dimensions the demon has access to, it IS true. It's kind of like saying 'it's five o'clock somewhere' - it's lying by omission, but technically it's not lying.<br /> <br /> Still, I kinda like the idea of those two abilities triggering rolls for cover. After all, making that kind of lie isn't lying to a particular entity - it's trying to pull a fast one on reality itself. Not only that, the changeling's powers make reality want to enforce itself a little more than usual, and in an unusual way. Reality itself would want to force the alien thing out. Mind you, this isn't the changeling's powers winning per say - the changeling will probably never know the lie was a lie - but the lie might have a cost on the demon trying to swing it. I'd probably add another roll for cover if the changeling gathered proof that the demon was lying.<br /> <br /> Out of curiosity, are there rules on the consequences of a pledge being removed if the lie is no longer a lie? I wonder how you'd handle it if the demon later admitted that he broke a pledge and then began lying that he broke the pledge later.<br /> <br /> *sidenote: this is just how I'd play it and I'm assuming one realistic way to interpret it. It goes without saying that this is ST discretion at this point, I just like discussing it because it's interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T11:54:15-07:00","id":117071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/113176-could-a-changeling-detect-a-demon-s-lies?p=116891#post116891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Which is why I changed my mind in a later, more descriptive post. Just two up from yours, in fact.<br /> <br /> <br /> Its not just the developers randomly saying things. Demons are liars by nature. Its a large part of what makes any demon a demon. That's just an in-game rationale for letting demons have demonic traits. Like Satchel said, Inferno has the same exact thing, with no more justification than &quot;These are demons.&quot;<br /> <br /> It may seem off to you because you just want there to be some way to break the whole perfect liar thing. Food for thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, still not buying it. Hilariously this is like the one thing in all of WoD that completely breaks immersion for me in how awkward it feels. Most things I can simply wave as game mechanics (even if I consider it a bad game mechanic) and not think a thing about it. Not this for some reason. It's not even overpowered/abusable or anything like a lot of things I harp on about since it would come up so rarely as to not even matter mechanically (which is also why I call bullshit on anyone claiming not having it breaks tension. It's not like demons or angels have the ability to do it so it <i>only</i> matters for crossovers).<br /> <br /> Spoofing comes pretty close to being the same way actually. Technically not overpowered but the way it plays out irks me like you wouldn't believe. That said, I can still hand wave spoofing. This, if it ever comes up, not so much.<br /> <br /> Let me attempt to put this into words It just feels...inappropriate isn't quite the right word. Hmm, I'm having trouble linking the feeling with a word, but it borders on inappropriate and out of place but not quite either of them. Simply put, it doesn't feel right. It doesn't feel like it should be a thing, and the fact that it <i>is</i> there is somewhat aggravating. The way it is currently doesn't even feel like perfect lying anymore. It's more like perfect lying + this-other-marginally-related-thing-that-seems-similar-enough-if-you-tilt-your-head-so-lets-include-it-anyways.<br /> <br /> Edit: Actually, let me ask this. Does this apply only if <i>directly</i> testing/scanning a demons statement for truth? As in, going, &quot;power, is that statement true?&quot;, or does it also apply to slightly more indirect inquiries? For example, lets say a demon tells a supernatural (lets say mage since I know how their powers work the best) the sky is orange. If the mage then uses a spell asking if the sky was orange, not whether the demon was lying or not, not really even attempting to analyze the demons words/intents/statements at all, would it register as being orange or not?<br /> <br /> Now then, lets say a demon tells a mage the sky is orange, a vampire right beside him also says the sky is orange, and the mage uses a spell to tell the validity of the vampires statements, does it still register as orange? If the answer is yes, what is the limitation to that? If the mage then called up a buddy who never heard the demons original statement asking them to check would it still register as orange? Would it then register as orange for everyone everywhere that tried to check?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 04-21-2014, 03:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T12:22:58-07:00","id":117090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/113176-could-a-changeling-detect-a-demon-s-lies?p=117071#post117071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now then, lets say a demon tells a mage the sky is orange, a vampire right beside him also says the sky is orange, and the mage uses a spell to tell the validity of the vampires statements, does it still register as orange? If the answer is yes, what is the limitation to that? If the mage then called up a buddy who never heard the demons original statement asking them to check would it still register as orange? Would it then register as orange for everyone everywhere that tried to check?</div> </div> </div> </div><i>The angry one leaned in and grabbed his phone from the dashboard. \u201cYou took a shot,\u201d she said. \u201cHope it works out for you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou \u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWasn\u2019t me,\u201d she said. \u201cYou said it. I just changed what you meant.\u201d She nodded up the street. \u201cI saw an ambulance about a block up. Think you can make it?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u200bJim\u2019s foot found the accelerator and the car started to move. He struggled to breathe, and tasted blood in his mouth. His grip on the steering wheel grew weak.<br /> <br /> \u200bBack at the bar, the demons dropped their expressions, becoming perfectly identical again. \u201cDid you really see an ambulance?\u201d one said.<br /> <br /> \u201cSure,\u201d said the other. \u201cYesterday.\u201d</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T12:55:18-07:00","id":117109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/113176-could-a-changeling-detect-a-demon-s-lies?p=117071#post117071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope, still not buying it. Hilariously this is like the one thing in all of WoD that completely breaks immersion for me in how awkward it feels. Most things I can simply wave as game mechanics (even if I consider it a bad game mechanic) and not think a thing about it. Not this for some reason. It's not even overpowered/abusable or anything like a lot of things I harp on about since it would come up so rarely as to not even matter mechanically (which is also why I call bullshit on anyone claiming not having it breaks tension. It's not like demons or angels have the ability to do it so it <i>only</i> matters for crossovers).<br /> <br /> Spoofing comes pretty close to being the same way actually. Technically not overpowered but the way it plays out irks me like you wouldn't believe. That said, I can still hand wave spoofing. This, if it ever comes up, not so much.<br /> <br /> Let me attempt to put this into words It just feels...inappropriate isn't quite the right word. Hmm, I'm having trouble linking the feeling with a word, but it borders on inappropriate and out of place but not quite either of them. Simply put, it doesn't feel right. It doesn't feel like it should be a thing, and the fact that it <i>is</i> there is somewhat aggravating. The way it is currently doesn't even feel like perfect lying anymore. It's more like perfect lying + this-other-marginally-related-thing-that-seems-similar-enough-if-you-tilt-your-head-so-lets-include-it-anyways.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly? Demon gets into a lot of quantum mechanics that can be hard to wrap your head around. If you're the type of person who must understand the physics behind the universe in order to enjoy immersion, you're probably going to need a primer on quantum physics before you're happy. I'm not trying to be elitist about it - I barely have a passing understanding of this stuff. We're talking about bending the rules of reality after all. But Demon does seem at least plausible with what little I've read on the subject.<br /> <br /> Think of it like this: a demon's reality is too big and complex to fit normally into ours. So, in order to interact and hide in our reality, it engineers a small new reality to hide in and transplants it into ours, like a geneticist might theoretically engineer an organ and transplant it into a human body. When the cover lies, the demon is subconsciously re-engineering the covers personal reality on the fly to make it true, despite true reality. When it spoofs, it's doing the opposite: it's subconsciously making the transplanted reality as close to the real reality as possible in the hopes that it'll mesh close enough that it's indistinguishable from reality. When it glitches, it's reality is being rejected by true reality and a side effect occurs, kind of like a transplanted organ might be rejected. Sometimes these side effects can be fixed (using our example, you might be able to use drugs to suppress the rejection of the organ) and sometimes they can not and the demon must start over with a new transplanted cover.<br /> <br /> I hope that helps. I've made a lot of weird comparisons over the years, but I never thought I'd be describing transplanting personal realities. lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1085,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","user":"Oddness","date":". 04-21-2014, 03:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T13:13:20-07:00","id":117117,"title":"","content":"To put it simply; the demon decides if he's testing as telling the truth or lying, not whether the statement itself tests as true.<br /> Demon says the sky is orange outside and the mage, who is inside, uses space to check, it's blue. Either the demon is lying or delusional.<br /> Demon says he's 29 (he's 208), the mage checks if he's telling the truth. He is.<br /> Demon says he killed someone (despite not even having left his room), mage checks, demon is telling the truth. Later on dead guy shows up, blazing away, mage flees, gets upset, goes back. &quot;I'm sorry! I really thought we got him!&quot; mage checks again, demon is telling the truth. If the mage went to that spot though, where the &quot;death&quot; should've taken place he wouldn't have found a corpse, and if he peered back through time he will see that the demon wasn't even there at the time of the alleged fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T13:39:09-07:00","id":117135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/113176-could-a-changeling-detect-a-demon-s-lies?p=117071#post117071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: Actually, let me ask this. Does this apply only if <i>directly</i> testing/scanning a demons statement for truth? As in, going, &quot;power, is that statement true?&quot;, or does it also apply to slightly more indirect inquiries? For example, lets say a demon tells a supernatural (lets say mage since I know how their powers work the best) the sky is orange. If the mage then uses a spell asking if the sky was orange, not whether the demon was lying or not, not really even attempting to analyze the demons words/intents/statements at all, would it register as being orange or not?</div> </div> </div> </div> Assuming that the spell is testing if the sky is X color independent of whatever the demon says, then, no, the result will come back blue (or whatever the sky really is). The conclusion to draw here is that the demon is either 1) insane, or 2) color blind and truthfully believes the sky is orange. You cannot test for objective facts here. It doesn't matter what the demon says here.<br /> <br /> If the demon says &quot;The sky is orange,&quot; and intends for it to be read as true, then the power detects that he truly believes the sky to be orange. It doesn't change reality. The mage, his magic, his mundane eyes, everything indicates that the man truly and utterly believes the sky to be orange. If he says &quot;the sky is blue&quot; and intends for it to be a lie, then people will see him act like a liar, a polygraph will record a lie, magic will detect the statement as a lie. <br /> <br /> <br /> Magic that works like a supernatural polygraph fails - demons have the tricks to beat that. Magic that works like a web page accessing wikipedia still works without fail. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now then, lets say a demon tells a mage the sky is orange, a vampire right beside him also says the sky is orange, and the mage uses a spell to tell the validity of the vampires statements, does it still register as orange? If the answer is yes, what is the limitation to that? If the mage then called up a buddy who never heard the demons original statement asking them to check would it still register as orange? Would it then register as orange for everyone everywhere that tried to check? </div> </div> </div> This makes no sense. A spell to tell the color of the sky will return the appropriate color (usually sky blue). It doesn't matter who says it. That's outside the scope of the power in question. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T13:54:59-07:00","id":117144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asaram</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/113176-could-a-changeling-detect-a-demon-s-lies?p=117117#post117117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demon says he's 29 (he's 208), the mage checks if he's telling the truth. He is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assume the Mage checks for truth by using a mind+space+time spell. The spell takes what the Mage has heard and uses the information to scry back in time to look at what actually happened (i.e. it looks at the place the Demon was born at the exact time it was born) and compares what the mage heard with what it scries. What does the spell report to the mage?<br /> It's a spell that checks the truth of a statement, but does that mean the Demon's ability presents the intelligence within the spell with a fake scenario, or does the intelligence see that there was noone borne at the time and place the Demon provided?<br /> Assume the spell can only inform the mage by using one of the two words &quot;truth&quot; and &quot;lie&quot; (the mage doesn't have enough Mind for more elaborate answers).<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: was mostly answered while writing this (yes, I took that long ^^)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":166,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","user":"Joker","date":". 04-21-2014, 04:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T13:56:53-07:00","id":117147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/113176-could-a-changeling-detect-a-demon-s-lies?p=117135#post117135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The conclusion to draw here is that the demon is either 1) insane, or 2) color blind and truthfully believes the sky is orange.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, as with the example of the twins above, 3) the demon is leaning on unstated qualifiers (<i>when</i> and <i>where </i>is the sky orange?) or 4) the demon is changing what either the question or the answer means to make the answer read as true or false.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 04-21-2014, 05:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T14:24:40-07:00","id":117164,"title":"","content":"It makes sense that, in a game of espionage, the way to find out if a demon is lying is to compare what he says to facts (ie the sky not being orange, the demon not having been at the murder scene). It hammers into home that if a mage or changeling wants to find the truth, they have to fact check and cross reference. Which also means that a demon lying about entirely subjective or internal things (his mood, how he feels, what he wants) will be entirely untraceable, save by observing their actions (and even then, the actions could be false leads). Long story short, if you want to figure out a demon's lies, it'll take more story/rap and fewer reliances on powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-21T23:22:26-07:00","id":117444,"title":"","content":"I think Asaram said it best...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asaram</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/113176-could-a-changeling-detect-a-demon-s-lies?p=114268#post114268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I would rule that if the pledge was sworn while in cover it's perfectly fine, the demon gets away with it, the COVER swore and the demon decides what they believe, if the demon swore in it's natural form, or as itself, then all bets are off, any attempt at telling a lie would break the pledge.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the demon is in-cover and swears the pledge, they can play with it as they please since the cover is essentially a finger-puppet that the demon controls the thoughts of. But, if the demon were to swear the pledge while in it's true form, then the pledge would take effect as intended.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T08:56:40-07:00","id":117478,"title":"","content":"One other thing to remember: if the demon says his cover is 29 and the mage checks through time, they'll probably get the covers age - not the demons. In theory, the demon could decide that the cover truly is 29 and minipulate reality of the cover in that scenario - turning it from a simple lie to a spoof.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-22T13:04:05-07:00","id":117586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/113176-could-a-changeling-detect-a-demon-s-lies?p=116806#post116806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The deceptive power of demons is written as if it wouldn't actually trigger a Clash of Wills. So no, it doesn't.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> It tends to happen with crossover games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for clarifying Neall, I subscribed as much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Assistant Organizer for:</b><br /> <a href=\"http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i162.photobucket.com/albums/t261/jlburgos_bucket/a41e98d1-1eed-4506-a8d2-2b3bea4a43da_zps469395ad.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/311-joeb","name":"JoeB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar311_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-23T00:13:22-07:00","id":117882,"title":"","content":"You guys make it sound like a Demon weaseling it's way out of a pledge by making every statement it makes to be true as far as reality is concerned (regardless of whether or not it actually is true) won't compromise it's ability to lie.<br /> <br /> Consider this; the Demon can never make any statement it makes to be a lie in that cover without breaking the pledge for the same reason that it can make any statement it wants to be the truth. Any lengthy supernatural mental or truth scrying of any sort over a period of time will inevitably reveal it's supernatural nature, of the &quot;most likely a Demon&quot; variety, because every statement they make will always ping as true no matter what over and over again unless it's willing to break the pledge.<br /> <br /> Unless the cover is disposable or it's the current &quot;Demon face&quot; it's going to eventually have to make a decision of whether or not to take the sanction or compromise it's &quot;perfect liar&quot; quality with that cover risking getting found out when it doesn't want to be found in that cover.<br /> <br /> *EDIT*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2111-doeman","user":"DoeMan","date":". 04-23-2014, 03:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2111-doeman","name":"DoeMan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-23T09:22:21-07:00","id":117946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DoeMan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/113176-could-a-changeling-detect-a-demon-s-lies?p=117882#post117882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You guys make it sound like a Demon weaseling it's way out of a pledge by making every statement it makes to be true as far as reality is concerned (regardless of whether or not it actually is true) won't compromise it's ability to lie.</div> </div> </div> </div> Its all white room theory crafting at this point, anyways. Its all stuff that won't come up in play at all.<br /> <br /> I mean, hells, what insane, convoluted situation would be happening where a mage would be attempting to catch a demon in a lie with magic with these bizarre questions? Its not something that would come up in play unless the Unchained has already had his cover made by the mage. In which case, the entire exercise would be pointless.<br /> <br /> It might not be a combat white room scenario, but it has all the same problems as one. And just as &quot;realistic.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Consider this; the Demon can never make any statement it makes to be a lie in that cover without breaking the pledge for the same reason that it can make any statement it wants to be the truth. Any lengthy supernatural mental or truth scrying of any sort over a period of time will inevitably reveal it's supernatural nature, of the &quot;most likely a Demon&quot; variety, because every statement they make will always ping as true no matter what over and over again unless it's willing to break the pledge. </div> </div> </div> Demons can make statements read as a lie if they want as they want. Any demon with half a brain can use it to maintain his cover against questions. And, again, I would want to know what kind of situation happens where the demon is in such a convoluted place<br /> .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 04-23-2014, 12:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-23T09:54:14-07:00","id":117964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/113176-could-a-changeling-detect-a-demon-s-lies?p=117946#post117946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demons can make statements read as a lie if they want as they want. Any demon with half a brain can use it to maintain his cover against questions. And, again, I would want to know what kind of situation happens where the demon is in such a convoluted place<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Me too. A game in which the Demon has to lie and have it read as a lie to help maintain his cover would make for one hell of an interesting, convoluted and well written adventure.<br /> <br /> But yeah, if the mage knew what he was looking for and trying to detect angels and demons, he might try some sort of spell to detect if the creature has ever lied. Anyone who reads as having told very few or no lies in his life would likely be flagged pretty easily...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-23T09:57:18-07:00","id":117968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oddness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/113176-could-a-changeling-detect-a-demon-s-lies?p=117964#post117964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But yeah, if the mage knew what he was looking for and trying to detect angels and demons, he might try some sort of spell to detect if the creature has ever lied. Anyone who reads as having told very few or no lies in his life would likely be flagged pretty easily...</div> </div> </div> </div> Demons tell lies all the time. Their covers tell lies. They tell truths that people interpret as lies. They tell lies people detect as truths. <br /> <br /> And the magic would likely rely on bits of mind reading, which the demon gets to determine what they pick up.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-23T21:53:37-07:00","id":118256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/113176-could-a-changeling-detect-a-demon-s-lies?p=117144#post117144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Assume the Mage checks for truth by using a mind+space+time spell. The spell takes what the Mage has heard and uses the information to scry back in time to look at what actually happened (i.e. it looks at the place the Demon was born at the exact time it was born) and compares what the mage heard with what it scries. What does the spell report to the mage?<br /> It's a spell that checks the truth of a statement, but does that mean the Demon's ability presents the intelligence within the spell with a fake scenario, or does the intelligence see that there was noone borne at the time and place the Demon provided?<br /> Assume the spell can only inform the mage by using one of the two words &quot;truth&quot; and &quot;lie&quot; (the mage doesn't have enough Mind for more elaborate answers).</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's a spell that would discover the nature of the Unchained, thus they get to spoof. Otherwise, it merely gets the Cover's age.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-24T09:59:23-07:00","id":118472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/113176-could-a-changeling-detect-a-demon-s-lies?p=116883#post116883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Longer answer provided by general mechanics of the NWoD -<br /> <br /> No. Perfect lying is part of the Demon base template and those abilities cannot be negated until a game line reaches tier 4 (cosmic) level powers e.g. Archmages, Ascended True Fae, Rank 6+ Angels, Spirits etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the Unchained can only be found out by creatures that:<br /> <br /> 1. One half is trying to become, and<br /> <br /> 2. At least Changelings try to AVOID becoming.<br /> <br /> Sounds like the same WTF moment when we found out that only Changelings and those that are touched can see through the Mask. Seems easy to keep an Unchained's Cover intact indefinitely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/891-jackalopevegas","name":"JackalopeVegas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-24T10:31:06-07:00","id":118489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/113176-could-a-changeling-detect-a-demon-s-lies?p=117968#post117968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Demons tell lies all the time. Their covers tell lies. They tell truths that people interpret as lies. They tell lies people detect as truths.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this is why a demon would still be constrained by such a truth-telling pledge. Whether they're lying or telling the truth is voluntary in a way that would be nonsensical to anyone else - so sure they'd be able to lie, have it read as true, and not trip the sanction - but sometimes, the convenient approach is to read as lying, and then they'll trip the sanction whether they are or not. So it's a pledge-clause that works differently on them, but still <i>does</i> work. It's hardly treading on changeling or in need of an extensive white room analysis.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-24T10:45:24-07:00","id":118497,"title":"","content":"So, most likely a demon would have the choice--trip the sanction if it becomes necessary, or fiddle with Fate and hope the changeling never catches you in a sanctioness lie. Free will can be a headache sometimes, as can being trapped in a world of lies. I agree, though, white rooming it is one thing but if it ever came up in play there would be other variables involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-25T06:14:12-07:00","id":119072,"title":"","content":"I think the original idea wasn't a sanction against lying, it was what happens when a demon trips a sanction but lies and says it didn't.<br /> <br /> For instance, if the pledge says 'don't steal cookies from the cookie jar' and they stole cookies from the cookie jar - then told everyone that they didn't and therefore aren't effected by the consequences of breaking the pledge. With this interpretation of the demon's lying ability, they can basically decide never to take the consequences of breaking a pledge. It's actually a pretty ridiculous application of the rules if you think of it like that.<br /> <br /> Again, in this scenario, I'd still say the demon wins but the lie would probably threaten their cover pretty badly if they got caught.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T09:43:35-07:00","id":119799,"title":"","content":"No, that wouldn't work. They can't change the universe with this ability, they ONLY change if what they say read as a lie or as them speaking truth. If they stole the cookie the pledge would be broken and they'd be hit with the sanction. If they then lied and said that they didn't steal it (and made it so this read as truth) they could at best confuse a changeling big time, but the sanction would still be tripped.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1734-asaram","name":"Asaram","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1734_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"331"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T08:00:25-07:00","id":120340,"title":"","content":"That... is very much out of the scope of the demon's lying power. When a human lies, their body inevitably betrays them. There are physical symptoms of telling a lie. You can try to mask them, you can try to obfuscate them, but they are always there, underneath. <br /> <br /> A demon's ability to lie is just to eliminate (or show when there would normally be none) those physical signs. This extends to magical polygraphs as well. That's it. This power basically can be summed up as &quot;I win all Subterfuge skill contests without ever rolling.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-27T09:56:38-07:00","id":120393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/113176-could-a-changeling-detect-a-demon-s-lies?p=114009#post114009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, the more I think on it, I'm going to change my answer to &quot;the demon wins.&quot; The pledge is no different than any other power in the world that can pull this off, and being a perfect liar is as much part of being a demon as using dreams are to a changeling.<br /> <br /> <br /> I don't like the idea that there's any power out there than can completely get past such an inextricable part of a supernatural's nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad you have seen the light.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Assistant Organizer for:</b><br /> <a href=\"http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i162.photobucket.com/albums/t261/jlburgos_bucket/a41e98d1-1eed-4506-a8d2-2b3bea4a43da_zps469395ad.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/311-joeb","name":"JoeB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar311_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}